message: >-
  If you use this code, these result tables, or these figures, please cite the
  work below. Attribution is a condition of the CC BY 4.0 licence.
title: >-
  Shared visual representation increases along the ventral hierarchy for semantic
  but not low-level features
abstract: >-
  Analysis code, derived result tables and manuscript source for a study of
  individual differences in visual cortical representation in the Natural Scenes
  Dataset. Per-participant decoders map voxels into a common feature space and
  are evaluated against a noise ceiling built from two decoders trained on
  disjoint halves of each participant's images. The shared fraction rises along
  the ventral hierarchy for a semantic target and is absent for a low-level
  target in the same voxels. No Natural Scenes Dataset data is redistributed.
